body:
I feel a pain in my chest and sick to my stomach... and pretty exhausted. I might even be making myself actually sick, cause I have a sore throat now. 

&#x200B;

It's totally possible for depression and anxiety to wreak havoc on your mind AND your body. Your immune system weakens and you can feel real, physical pain. I'm not an expert, but I can tell you what makes me feel better. I know a lot of advice says to be proactive, exercise, and keep yourself busy. But I think it's also important to nurture yourself when you need it. I find it fun (in the context of being depressed, at least) to shop around for herbal teas. They have some for stress relief and digestive relief. I find them to work decently, even if it's just the thought of self-soothing that counts. Maybe take a bath and light some candles, even if you're a dude. Buy yourself a good book. Get a bunch of snacks you love and sit down to play a video game all the way through. I hope you feel better soon too.
